# What a result may be, in the terms of the function that is asked: a parameter, a literal, an operator of those, a read, an object that was made for the call.
# What a callee answers is put into the caller's terms: for a parameter of the callee stands what the call passes. The records are written by hand: some say more than their bodies do.
# The table keeps a result that names a parameter or that may be an object which nobody else holds. Flow says the rest of every call at once.
# RUN: relational-summary
# CHECK-LABEL: f1
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0] | o0 = parameter 0
# CHECK-LABEL: f2
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 1 | o1 = String f2 v3
# CHECK-LABEL: f3
# CHECK: result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = parameter 1 | o2 = Add(o0, o1)
# The operator of the callee, of what this call passes
# CHECK-LABEL: f4
# CHECK: result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Integer f4 v1 | o2 = Add(o0, o1)
# Fresh through a factory that calls a factory, with the calls that lead down to the operation. Kept in a variable on the way up, it is neither fresh nor are its stores listed
# CHECK-LABEL: f5
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f5 v0 held-by-nobody-else holds {}
# CHECK-LABEL: f6
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f5 v0 held-by-nobody-else through f6 v0 holds {}
# CHECK-LABEL: f7
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f5 v0 held-by-nobody-else through f7 v0 through f6 v0 holds {}
# CHECK-LABEL: f8
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = NewObject f5 v0 through f8 v1
# CHECK-NOT: holds
# A function that hands its parameter on to itself answers that parameter. One that adds to it at each level comes to rest at the deepest origin, whose operand is anything
# CHECK-LABEL: f9
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0] | o0 = parameter 1
# CHECK-LABEL: f10
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o2, o3, o4, o5, o6, o7, o8, o10] | o0 = parameter 1 | o1 = Integer f10 v3 | o2 = Add(o0, o1) | o3 = Add(o2, o1)
# CHECK: | o8 = Add(o7, o1) | o9 = anything | o10 = Add(o9, o1)
# A parameter that a call by value has no argument for is undefined
# CHECK-LABEL: f12
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Undefined
# An operand that nobody lists leaves the operator listed
# CHECK-LABEL: f13
# CHECK: result0: one of [o3] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = PropGet o0 k{{*}} | o2 = anything | o3 = Greater(o1, o2)
# Anything: a coroutine answers a promise (the link says nothing of it at all), an argument may be a value that is not listed.
# `new` of a plain function answers the object that was made, unless the function returns one: an object that nobody lists
# CHECK-NOT: f14
# CHECK-LABEL: f15
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = anything of t8
# CHECK-LABEL: f16
# CHECK-NOT: result0
# Two functions that call each other
# CHECK-LABEL: f17
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 1 | o1 = parameter 2
# CHECK-LABEL: f18
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 2 | o1 = parameter 1
# The computed key of a read is its operand: listed by the record, a literal in the body, what a caller passes
# CHECK-LABEL: f19
# CHECK: result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = parameter 1 | o2 = ElemGet o0(o1)
# CHECK-LABEL: f20
# CHECK: result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Integer f20 v1 | o2 = ElemGet o0(o1)
# CHECK-LABEL: f21
# CHECK: result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Integer f21 v1 | o2 = ElemGet o0(o1)
# No call returns: nothing that depends on the call. `return;`. Not all listed. More origins than a result may have: the function has no parameter either, so it is not printed
# CHECK-LABEL: f22
# CHECK-NOT: result0
# CHECK-LABEL: f23
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Undefined
# CHECK-LABEL: f24
# CHECK-NOT: result0
# CHECK-NOT: f25
# What was stored into the object, with what the call passes in place of the factory's parameters
# CHECK-LABEL: f26
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f26 v2 held-by-nobody-else holds {[[x]]: o1, [[y]]?: o2} | o1 = parameter 0 | o2 = parameter 1
# CHECK-LABEL: f27
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f26 v2 held-by-nobody-else through f27 v2 holds {[[x]]: o1, [[y]]?: o2} | o1 = parameter 0 | o2 = Integer f27 v1
# Made here, one call below, or further down, where the way is no longer listed
# CHECK-LABEL: f28
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0, o1, o2] | o0 = NewObject f28 v3 held-by-nobody-else holds {} | o1 = NewObject f28 v3 held-by-nobody-else through f28 v2 holds {} | o2 = NewObject f28 v3 held-by-nobody-else through-unlisted-calls
# The callees that flow lists at a call by value. As an operand they are one origin
# CHECK-LABEL: f31
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1, o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Integer f29 v0 | o2 = Integer f30 v0
# CHECK-LABEL: f32
# CHECK: result0: one of [o4] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Integer f29 v0 | o2 = Integer f30 v0 | o3 = one of (o0, o1, o2) | o4 = Add(o3, o0)
# A built-in function: receiver and arguments
# CHECK-LABEL: f33
# CHECK: result0: one of [o3] | o0 = Undefined | o1 = parameter 0 | o2 = parameter 1 | o3 = builtin {{*}}(o0, o1, o2)
# The fields that a literal fills have their keys
# CHECK-LABEL: f34
# CHECK: result0: fresh one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f34 v2 held-by-nobody-else holds {[[x]] = o1, [[y]] = o2} | o1 = parameter 0 | o2 = parameter 1
# A value that is called and of which nobody can say here what it is: what is called, the receiver, the arguments. A caller puts its closure in
# CHECK-LABEL: f35
# CHECK: result0: one of [o3] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Undefined | o2 = parameter 1 | o3 = call(o0, o1, o2)
# CHECK-LABEL: f36
# CHECK: result0: one of [o3] | o0 = NewClosure f36 v1{{*}} | o1 = Undefined | o2 = parameter 0 | o3 = call(o0, o1, o2)
# What a closure has captured stands for the capture where the closure is called by the function that made it
# CHECK-LABEL: f38
# CHECK: result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 1 | o1 = parameter 0 | o2 = Add(o0, o1)
# Of a callee whose result is not listed there is the type that flow has proven of it: the parameter beside it is not lost
# CHECK-LABEL: f40
# CHECK: result0: one of [o0, o1] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = anything of t
# Before flow has run no callee is followed: a call by value is said in terms of what is called, a direct call is not listed, nothing is said of who holds an object,
# and the stores are those that the function makes itself
# RUN(BEFORE): origins-before-flow
# BEFORE: f3 result0: one of [o2] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = parameter 1 | o2 = Add(o0, o1)
# BEFORE-NOT: f4 result0
# BEFORE: f5 result0: one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f5 v0
# BEFORE-NOT: held-by-nobody-else
# BEFORE: f12 result0: one of [o0, o3] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = NewClosure f12 v1 | o2 = Undefined | o3 = call(o1, o2, o0)
# BEFORE: f26 result0: one of [o0] | o0 = NewObject f26 v2 holds at least {[[x]]: o1, [[y]]?: o2} | o1 = parameter 0 | o2 = parameter 1
# BEFORE: f31 result0: one of [o0, o5] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = NewClosure f31 v2 | o2 = NewClosure f31 v3 | o3 = Undefined | o4 = one of (o1, o2) | o5 = call(o4, o3)
# BEFORE: f35 result0: one of [o3] | o0 = parameter 0 | o1 = Undefined | o2 = parameter 1 | o3 = call(o0, o1, o2)

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
layout L0 name="Empty"
layout L1 name="Pair" fields=[{key="x" declared={type=anything}}, {key="y" declared={type=anything}}]
